<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Mac dependency auto-sync — LaunchAgent (2026-08-11).

  Runs scripts/mac_auto_sync.sh: build the three artifacts only the Mac can
  build (sector index bars, darling valuation, bars cache) and push them to
  the VM. The VM builds everything else from its own bhavcopy.

  WHY A LaunchAgent AND NOT CRON. macOS cron does not fire while the machine
  is asleep and does not catch up afterwards — audited 2026-08-04, the Mac's
  bhavcopy job silently missed 4 of 11 weekdays with no log line at all on the
  missed days. launchd is the opposite: RunAtLoad fires at every login, and a
  StartInterval tick missed while asleep is COALESCED and fires on wake. That
  is exactly the "sync whenever the laptop is opened" behaviour wanted here.

  INSTALL — run these three lines on the Mac:

    cp scripts/com.aditrader.sync.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.aditrader.sync.plist
    launchctl enable gui/$(id -u)/com.aditrader.sync

  VERIFY:
    launchctl list | grep aditrader
    launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.aditrader.sync   # force one run now
    tail -f logs/mac_auto_sync.log logs/mac_auto_sync.launchd.err

  UNINSTALL:
    launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.aditrader.sync
    rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.aditrader.sync.plist

  ⚠️ /bin/bash MUST HOLD FULL DISK ACCESS (System Settings -> Privacy &
  Security -> Full Disk Access). launchd-spawned bash cannot read a repo
  inside ~/Documents without it and fails with "Operation not permitted" —
  the edge miner lost a day to exactly this on 2026-07-09. It is already
  granted on this Mac; a macOS upgrade can silently revoke it, so if this
  agent goes quiet, check that FIRST.

  StartInterval is 3600s, but the script throttles itself to one real run per
  3 hours (data/.mac_auto_sync_state) — these are DAILY producers, and a
  yfinance sweep every hour would be rude to Yahoo and useless to us. The
  agent may therefore fire often and do nothing, which is the intended shape:
  cheap ticks, occasional work, and a sync within an hour of the lid opening.

  Paths are absolute by launchd requirement; adjust if the repo moves.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.aditrader.sync</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/adityagupta/Documents/Claude/alpha_trading/scripts/mac_auto_sync.sh</string>
    </array>

    <!-- Fires at every login/agent load — i.e. when the machine comes up. -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- Hourly while awake; a tick missed during sleep coalesces to wake. -->
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>3600</integer>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/adityagupta/Documents/Claude/alpha_trading</string>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/adityagupta/Documents/Claude/alpha_trading/logs/mac_auto_sync.launchd.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/adityagupta/Documents/Claude/alpha_trading/logs/mac_auto_sync.launchd.err</string>

    <!-- Nice: this is background housekeeping, never worth a spinning fan. -->
    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
    <key>LowPriorityIO</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
